research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-t7-examples.log-35-DEFECT: Countable choice selects one finite subfamily for each compact piece, but those finite subfamilies have not been simultaneously enumerated. L4 concerns enumeration of one nonempty at-most-countable set and does not prove that a countable union of arbitrary finite sets is countable. A further use of countable choice is needed, contrary to the assertion that choice is spent once.  
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-t7-examples.log-36-EVIDENCE: `lem-countable-iff-surjection-from-n` addresses one nonempty set. The separate target `thm-countable-union-of-countable` begins, “Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice,” and is the result that licenses the union step; it is absent from this item’s dependencies and facts.  
